### void QDataStream::setFloatingPointPrecision([QDataStream::FloatingPointPrecision](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatastream.html#FloatingPointPrecision-enum) *precision*)

Sets the floating point precision of the data stream to *precision*. If the floating
point precision is
[DoublePrecision](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatastream.html#FloatingPointPrecision-enum)
and the version of the data stream is
[Qt\\_4\\_6](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatastream.html#Version-enum) or higher,
all floating point numbers will be written and read with 64-bit precision. If the
floating point precision is
[SinglePrecision](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatastream.html#FloatingPointPrecision-enum)
and the version is
[Qt\\_4\\_6](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatastream.html#Version-enum) or higher,
all floating point numbers will be written and read with 32-bit precision.

For versions prior to
[Qt\\_4\\_6](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatastream.html#Version-enum), the
precision of floating point numbers in the data stream depends on the stream operator
called.

The default is
[DoublePrecision](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatastream.html#FloatingPointPrecision-enum).

Note that this property does not affect the serialization or deserialization of
`qfloat16` instances.

**Warning:** This property must be set to the same value on the object that writes and
