## Detailed Description

A QRegularExpressionMatchIterator object is a forward only Java-like iterator; it can be
obtained by calling the
[QRegularExpression::globalMatch](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qregularexpression.html#globalMatch)()
function. A new QRegularExpressionMatchIterator will be positioned before the first
result. You can then call the
[hasNext](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qregularexpressionmatchiterator.html#hasNext)()
function to check if there are more results available; if so, the
[next](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qregularexpressionmatchiterator.html#next)()
function will return the next result and advance the iterator.

Each result is a
[QRegularExpressionMatch](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qregularexpressionmatch.html)
object holding all the information for that result (including captured substrings).

For instance:

```
// extracts the words
QRegularExpression re("(\\\\w+)");
QString subject("the quick fox");
QRegularExpressionMatchIterator i = re.globalMatch(subject);
while (i.hasNext()) {
    QRegularExpressionMatch match = i.next();
    // ...
}
```

Moreover, QRegularExpressionMatchIterator offers a
[peekNext](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qregularexpressionmatchiterator.html#peekNext)()
function to get the next result *without* advancing the iterator.

You can retrieve the
[QRegularExpression](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qregularexpression.html) object
the subject string was matched against by calling the
[regularExpression](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qregularexpressionmatchiterator.html#regularExpression)()
function; the match type and the match options are available as well by calling the
[matchType](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qregularexpressionmatchiterator.html#matchType)()
and the
[matchOptions](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qregularexpressionmatchiterator.html#matchOptions)()
respectively.

Please refer to the
[QRegularExpression](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qregularexpression.html)
documentation for more information about the Qt regular expression classes.

