## Detailed Description

QSaveFile is an I/O device for writing text and binary files, without losing existing
data if the writing operation fails.

While writing, the contents will be written to a temporary file, and if no error
happened, [commit](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsavefile.html#commit)() will move
it to the final file. This ensures that no data at the final file is lost in case an
error happens while writing, and no partially-written file is ever present at the final
location. Always use QSaveFile when saving entire documents to disk.

QSaveFile automatically detects errors while writing, such as the full partition
situation, where [write](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qiodevice.html#write)()
cannot write all the bytes. It will remember that an error happened, and will discard
the temporary file in
[commit](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsavefile.html#commit)().

Much like with [QFile](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qfile.html), the file is
opened with [open](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsavefile.html#open)(). Data is
usually read and written using
[QDataStream](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qdatastream.html) or
[QTextStream](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qtextstream.html), but you can also
call the [QIODevice](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qiodevice.html)-inherited
functions [read](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qiodevice.html#read)(),
[readLine](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qiodevice.html#readLine)(),
[readAll](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qiodevice.html#readAll)(),
[write](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qiodevice.html#write)().

Unlike [QFile](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qfile.html), calling
[close](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qfiledevice.html#close)() is not allowed.
[commit](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsavefile.html#commit)() replaces it. If
[commit](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsavefile.html#commit)() was not called and
the QSaveFile instance is destroyed, the temporary file is discarded.

To abort saving due to an application error, call
[cancelWriting](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsavefile.html#cancelWriting)(), so
that even a call to [commit](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsavefile.html#commit)()
