### void QSize::scale(int *width*, int *height*, [Qt::AspectRatioMode](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#AspectRatioMode-enum) *mode*)

Scales the size to a rectangle with the given *width* and *height*, according to the
specified *mode*:

- If *mode* is [Qt::IgnoreAspectRatio](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#AspectRatioMode-enum), the size is set to (*width*, *height*).
- If *mode* is [Qt::KeepAspectRatio](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#AspectRatioMode-enum), the current size is scaled to a rectangle as large as possible inside (*width*, *height*), preserving the aspect ratio.
- If *mode* is [Qt::KeepAspectRatioByExpanding](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qt.html#AspectRatioMode-enum), the current size is scaled to a rectangle as small as possible outside (*width*, *height*), preserving the aspect ratio.

Example:

```
QSize t1(10, 12);
t1.scale(60, 60, Qt::IgnoreAspectRatio);
// t1 is (60, 60)

QSize t2(10, 12);
t2.scale(60, 60, Qt::KeepAspectRatio);
// t2 is (50, 60)

QSize t3(10, 12);
t3.scale(60, 60, Qt::KeepAspectRatioByExpanding);
// t3 is (60, 72)
```

**See also** [setWidth](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsize.html#setWidth)(),
[setHeight](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsize.html#setHeight)(), and
[scaled](https://doc.qt.io/archives/qt-5.15/qsize.html#scaled)().

