### bool QUrl::isValid() const

Returns `true` if the URL is non-empty and valid; otherwise returns `false`.

The URL is run through a conformance test. Every part of the URL must conform to the
standard encoding rules of the URI standard for the URL to be reported as valid.

```
bool checkUrl(const QUrl &url) {
    if (!url.isValid()) {
        qDebug("Invalid URL: %s", qUtf8Printable(url.toString()));
        return false;
    }

    return true;
}
```

